    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1942986841214398497",
      "url": "https://x.com/followlastma/status/1942986841214398497",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/followlastma/status/1942986841214398497",
      "text": "[5:33PM] #TrafficUpdate #Oshodi #Mushin \n\n Vehicular movement from Moshalasi, near the Alakara police station, down to Idi Oro is flowing smoothly. The areas around Conoil at Idi Oro, Olosha, Ogunmokun junction, Ojuwoye Post Office, and down to Cappa are experiencing very good traffic conditions. Additionally, the route from Olupese in Oshodi, underneath the bridge, through the Oshodi train station, Brown junction, and down to the Arena is reporting steady movement.\n\nThe return journey from Bolade Oshodi, through Brown junction to Goro, is currently clear. Traffic along Oshodi Oke descending towards Goro by Terminal 2 is moving smoothly. Similarly, the ascent from Oshodi underneath the bridge to Oshodi Oke by Terminal 1 is good.\n\n The route from Olupese and Cappa down to Ojuwoye is clear for traffic. Furthermore, the connection from Ojuwoye onto Isolo Road, leading to Palm Avenue, is currently steady.  The Oye Roundabout inwards towards LASUTECH is experiencing moving traffic, as is the return journey from the Daleko Bridge. \n\nIn Zone D, the Pako junction is functioning as expected, with steady movement reported from Alasalatu down through Mushin Ile Epo Isale, with a slight slowdown noted at the turning. Overall, traffic inward Idi Oro down to Moshalasi is good. There are no impediments reported, and officers are present and managing the flow.\n\n#followLASTMA",
