    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1942988559062835682",
      "url": "https://x.com/followlastma/status/1942988559062835682",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/followlastma/status/1942988559062835682",
      "text": "[5:40PM] #Alausa #Ikeja #TrafficUpdate \n\nObafemi Awolowo Way is currently experiencing good flow from Barrack, through Coca-Cola junction, Radio, and Allen junction to Balogun. However, there is congestion from Olowu inwards Ikeja underneath the bridge due to the spillover from the Ikeja Along overpass. While the return journey is generally good, traffic becomes busy as vehicles approach Allen junction and Radio junction.\n\nLateef Jakande Road is moving at a faster pace, but experiences heavy traffic from Cadbury through Agidingbi first gate, Wemco, to Omole Roundabout. Despite the volume, traffic flow is maintained. Aromire Road, connecting Adeniyi Jones, Akora Villa, and Hacco, is busy. The return journey on this corridor is good, but traffic thickens approaching Allen junction.\n\nOther key corridors within the zone, including Mobolaji Johnson Avenue from the Old Tollgate through 7up, Billingsway to Alausa intersection, and the stretch of Dr Nurudeen Olowopopo leading towards Otedola underneath the bridge, are currently reporting good traffic conditions. \n\nNo impediments have been recorded, and officers are actively managing the flow of vehicles.\n\n#FollowLASTMA",
